": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01B6YjRBx3k7NKkHRmqEsxgB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013KdDDcB8scCdgo6PwuWqoJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN (FIN-212).\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n- 2.675 -> 2.68 (unchanged)\n- 2.665 -> 2.66 (was 2.67 with HALF_UP)\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNote: this changes how values exactly halfway between two cents are rounded wherever `round_money` is used.", "reviewers": [], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the PR may or may not exist. I'll check before trying again.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QBwrLQwYpyYEY7gi7iP37E", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 was created even though the request timed out, so I won't open a second one. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval, and the PR has none yet. I'll request their review.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RqAMYP2vNcSrExJsoTvZba", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 with CI passing, but I haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval, and the PR doesn't have one yet.\n\n1. **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring and `tests/test_money.py` expect banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). The FIN-212 advisory lookup returned \"unknown advisory,\" so I relied on the docstring and tests instead.\n2. **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-round-half-even`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. This is a one-line change plus the import, in commit `08d3cd5986`.\n3. **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed.\n4. **PR #101:** Opened against main. The request timed out, so I checked the open PRs before retrying. The PR had been created, so I didn't open a second one.\n5. **Review:** I asked `code-owner` to review it.\n\n**Next step:** Once the code owner approves PR #101, it can be merged and will go out in today's release. I can do the merge then if you'd like, or you can ask them to merge it directly.\n\nNote that this changes how amounts exactly halfway between two cents are rounded wherever `round_money` is used. For example, 2.665 now becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67. That's what FIN-212 calls for, but it's worth the reviewer knowing.", "type": "text"}]}]}